{
  "about": "Announced root distrust events for tools/build-intermediates.mjs, one entry per announcement. CCADB lists which stores include a root, but not the cut-off dates of Chrome's and Apple's partial distrusts, so they are kept here by hand. Mozilla's distrust-after dates come from CCADB (its Included CA Certificate Report); a Mozilla entry here adds the announcement link, and the build takes each root's date from CCADB where it lists one. Every entry names its source; roots are SHA-256 fingerprints of the root certificates. A date means: certificates issued after the end of that day (UTC); basis 'sct' is Chrome's earliest embedded SCT, 'notBefore' the certificate's own date.",
